Ideas adapted, in our own words
-------------------------------

No text below was copied; these projects shaped the guidance and are credited
with thanks.

- anthropics/skills, skills/frontend-design (Apache License 2.0,
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0): plan-then-critique process,
  palette as named values, the calibration list of generated-looking defaults,
  restraint and writing guidance. Used in references/design.md.
- vercel-labs/web-interface-guidelines (MIT): pre-delivery checklist items.
  Used in references/checklist.md.
- warpdotdev/common-skills, readout (MIT): the zero-external-reference
  contract and the parse-and-scan delivery check. Used in scripts/check.py.
- nicobailon/visual-explainer (MIT): one claim per figure, labeled arrows,
  narrow and wide viewport checks, file:// pitfalls.
- plannotator/effective-html (MIT): page-type routing and the
  neighboring-topic originality check.
- zarazhangrui/frontend-slides (MIT): the fixed 1920x1080 stage scaled to the
  window. Used in assets/deck.html (independent implementation).
- tt-a1i/archify (MIT): never claim a visual check that was not performed.
- pbakaus/impeccable (Apache License 2.0): reading-column measure.
- Claude Code's built-in artifact guidance: general principles only (token
  plan, designed dark mode, diagram mechanics), restated independently.
